  "term": "transplacental transmission",
  "definition": "Transplacental transmission is the passage of an infectious agent from a pregnant mother across the placenta to the fetus, resulting in fetal infection. In the source material, it refers to virus reaching developing offspring before birth and sometimes causing pathological changes.",
